{
  "name": "glass-map — shipped pairings, Map pass (2026-07-04)",
  "_doc": [
    "Self-contained AA declaration for the Map screen glass pass. Every color is the SHIPPED value copied from src/theme.ts (light) + src/theme/ThemeContext.tsx darkColor (dark) + the inline literals in MapScreen.tsx / PlatformMap.tsx / PlatformMap.web.tsx / HeatmapLegend.tsx. Run: node <material-lab>/2026-07-02/shared/contrast-check.mjs map-stacks.json — must exit 0.",
    "BASES: the map backdrop is unbounded (tiles are independent of the JS theme — iOS Apple tiles follow the OS, web CartoDB dark_all is always dark). So every themed surface is declared over #000 AND #FFF in BOTH modes, plus the 5 heat saturants. Bases MUST be opaque (arbiter throws otherwise); all translucency lives in `stack`.",
    "WINDOW RULE: extremes are the true worst case IFF the ink luminance lies outside [Y(stack over #000), Y(stack over #FFF)]. Not hand-asserted — the arbiter probes every declared base and takes the true minimum, so an inside-window ink would surface as a sub-floor ratio here and be flagged. None did.",
    "LITERAL-ENGINEERED SURFACES: the pill + action bar ship as variant=row forceEngineered (a 0.92->0.84 light / 0.94->0.88 dark gradient), but are declared here against the THINNER true-blur row floor (0.70 / 0.72). That is the conservative bound — it covers the engineered arm too. The filter panel threads glassLite so it is blur (full) or engineered (C-lite); mapPaneWash (0.70/0.72 + 0.30 wash) is the conservative floor for both.",
    "RT NEVER CREDITS THE WASH: the GlassSurface Reduce-Transparency path returns before the overlayTint layer, so alwaysLightRT (0.95) and listFab (0.97) are declared WITHOUT the 0.30 wash. The panel under RT is the 0.97 opaque light fill, which out-contrasts floor+wash anyway.",
    "BOUNDARY = UNION, NOT A TEXT GUARANTEE: cluster rings + heat-badge edge can't span the range with one color, so they use dilution regimes — the heat ramp at HEATMAP_FILL_OPACITY 0.65 pre-composited over #000 (darkRegime) and #FFF (lightRegime), fed as opaque bases. The white ring covers backdrops Y<=0.30; the #0F1B2D hairline covers Y>=0.13; union covers all. These 3.0-floor union members are NOT a 4.5 text guarantee.",
    "HEAT BADGE RESIDUAL (disclosed, NEEDS-DEVICE): the badge EDGE (#0F1B2D) carries the light regime and the fill-keyed INK (>=4.59 vs its own fill) carries identification. Over the badge's OWN cell fill on dark tiles the badge BOUNDARY can drop below 3:1 for sev3-5 — accepted because the badge is a non-interactive text label (1.4.11 boundary not strictly required) and the ink is the identifier.",
    "F1 SCRIM: Sky picked NONE, so no scrim is shipped and none is declared. (Had the 0.12 top-edge gradient been chosen it would be excluded from every stack — it maps all bases strictly inside the declared windows, i.e. pure bonus.)",
    "F4 LIST FAB: KEPT on the themed color.brand ink (light #1466E0 / dark #4E89EF on the dark 0.97 overlay = 5.04) — NOT swapped to ctaFill, which would drop dark to 3.28. This pair is the canary for that guard."
  ],
